title: $:/plugins/lasjoh-toho/pinboard/readme

The ''Pinboard'' engine turns a [[TW5-Graph|$:/plugins/flibbles/graph]] graph into an infinite canvas: nodes become cards that show the fields you choose, you can draw and add shapes around them, and a path through the board plays back as a zooming, fullscreen presentation.

!! Getting started

Pick the template ''Pinboard (infinite canvas & presentation)'' in a graph's settings, or write the graph yourself:

```
<$graph $engine="Pinboard" store="My Board">
  <$list filter="[tag[Idea]]">
    <$node.default />
  </$list>
</$graph>
```

The `store` property names the tiddler that keeps the board's drawings, card sizes, chosen fields, background and presentation path (in its `pinboard` field). With the Pinboard template, that is the graph tiddler itself, which then holds everything about the board: the list of cards (`filter`), their positions (its text), and the `pinboard` field. Only the cards' content lives in their own tiddlers. Without a store, drawings only last until the board is re-rendered.

!! Menus

* ''Drawing dock'' (left, one narrow column). Each group opens a flyout to the side with its tools, colors and a size slider:
** ''Draw'': pencil, brush, Bezier curve (click points, double-click to finish)
** ''Shapes'': circle/ellipse, rectangle, polygon (click corners, double-click or click the first corner to close), line, arrow; fill on/off
** ''Text'': text with font size
** ''Sticky note'': note colors
** then eraser, new tiddler card, undo/redo. Click the active tool again to go back to selecting.
* ''Navigation'' (bottom center): select, pan, the ''Lupe'' (zoom slider, show everything, show the selection, 100%, hide images, and a ''filter'': words hide every card and note that does not contain them all, a `[filter[expression]]` keeps just the cards it selects; Enter or "Show matches" flies there), ''background'' (color; pattern none/dots/grid/lines; picture from a tiddler or URL, either fixed to the view or lying on the board with its own size) and ''fullscreen'' (the board fills the screen; TiddlyWiki's dialogs still open on top).
* ''Presentation'' (top right): ▶ present, presentation path (with the frame tool), layers.

!! Cards

* Drag a card to move it, drag its corner to resize it. Click an image to open it in a lightbox (fit or 1:1, scroll and drag to look around, Ctrl+wheel zooms).
* Hover a card for its tools: ''view'' (reader that is as tall as the tiddler, up to the whole screen; Edit/Close and "open in story river" appear on hover), ''add to path'', ''fields'', ''link'' (then click the card to link to), ''appear/disappear'', ''leads into board'', ''remove'' – two rows of icons right on the card's top edge.
* ''Fields'' chooses which fields this card shows and in which order. `title` toggles the card's heading; `text` renders the tiddler's body; `tags`, `created`/`modified`, `icon` get special treatment; any other field is shown as name and rendered value.
* ''Long tiddlers'': with `text` chosen, pick how much text the card shows on the board (whole text, up to the first `<br>` or blank line, the first image, or first image + text up to the first break) and, separately, in the presentation. A "more…" link opens the whole tiddler. Graph defaults: `textMode`, `presentTextMode`.
* Double-click a card to view it (unless the graph gives nodes their own `actions`). Drag the dot on a card's right edge to another card to connect them.
* Adding a tiddler (double-click on the board, or the card tool): type a title; if it does not exist yet, ''Create'' makes it.

!! Drawing

|Key |Tool |
|V |Select and move |
|H / Space |Pan |
|P |Pen |
|M |Highlighter |
|E |Eraser |
|R / O |Rectangle / ellipse (Shift: square / circle) |
|L / A |Line / arrow (Shift: 45° steps) |
|T |Text |
|N |Sticky note |
|B |Bezier curve (Enter or Esc finishes) |
|G |Polygon |
|F |Presentation frame |
|C |Add a tiddler card |

Selected shapes can be recolored, resized, rotated, moved with the arrow keys, sent behind or above the cards and deleted; Ctrl+D duplicates. A sticky note can be ''turned into a tiddler'' (first line = title, the rest = text, note color = tiddler color); it takes the note's place on the board. Double-click a shape to edit its text. Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z undo and redo. Mouse wheel or pinch zooms, `0` fits everything.

''Layers'' (presentation menu) lists every drawing, shape, note and frame from top to bottom, with the cards in between. Drag a row's grip to restack it, past the cards to move it behind or in front of them; the eye hides it from board and presentation.

!! Boards inside boards

A card whose tiddler has a `pinboard-dive` field naming another board tiddler leads into that board (set it with the card tool ''Leads into board'' (map icon): pick a board, or make a new empty one named after the card; boards open above are greyed out): its card looks like a little stack, and the first tool on hover (''dive'') shows that board in place of this one, with a breadcrumb above it (`Map › Start › …`) to go back up. Each board keeps its own positions and drawings. A card that leads to a board already open above it (directly or further up) cannot be dived into — its dive button is greyed out — so boards never nest inside themselves. Diving needs the Pinboard template; the template keeps the path in a state tiddler (`$:/state/pinboard/dive…`, the graph property `diveState`).

!! Presenting

Frames join the presentation path automatically. Cards, shapes and the current view can be added from their tools (play button in a circle) or the path panel (list icon, top right), where stops are reordered by dragging their grip. ▶ starts the presentation: fullscreen, camera flights between stops.

* ''Tilted stops'': rotate a frame (or any box shape) with the round handle above it (Shift: 15° steps). The camera turns with it on arrival.
* ''Appear / disappear'': the eye icon on a shape or card picks the stop at which it appears and the stop at which it disappears.
* ''Reveals'': shapes lying on top of a card or shape vanish while the presentation shows what they cover, so a sticky note can hide an answer until its stop.
* ''Progress stack'': hover the counter at the bottom to see every stop as a bar (the last on top). Hover a bar for a live preview, click to jump.
* ''Pen'': the pen at the bottom left (or `P`) writes temporary notes on top of the presentation: pen, highlighter, text, eraser, colors, size, clear. Notes zoom with the board and are not saved.
* Cards set to show more text in the presentation grow to their fuller version when the presentation stops at them.
* Keys: arrows/Space/Enter, Home/End, `O` overview, `F` fullscreen on/off (also a button in the bar), `P` pen, Esc to leave. Clicks at the left/right screen edges step back and forth; drag and wheel explore freely.
* ''Export as HTML'' (path panel) downloads a single self-contained file that plays the presentation in any browser, without TiddlyWiki. It uses the very same player.

!! Stories

A board can hold several presentation paths, called stories. The path panel shows one at a time: pick it at the top, the eye hides or shows its thread on the board, and ''+'' adds a story. The gear opens the story's settings: its name, the color and thickness of its thread, its story tiddler (''Make a story tiddler'' / ''Open story'') and ''Delete story''. ▶, the stops you add and ''Export as HTML'' all belong to the story shown.

* ''The thread'': while the path panel is open, the story is drawn on the board as a smooth line in its color from stop to stop, with each stop's number, and its cards get a ring in that color.
* ''Outline'': Tab / Shift+Tab on a stop in the panel (or the arrows on hover) indent and outdent it, so stops become sub-points of the one above.
* ''Open as story'' (under the story's name) puts the story's tiddlers in order at the top of the story river, without needing a story tiddler.
* ''Story tiddler'': the ''Tiddler'' field under the story's name (by default the board's and the story's name) names it before it is made; ''Make a story tiddler'' (or Enter) ties the story to it. Naming an existing tiddler uses that one (''Use this tiddler''); if it already holds a story, you are asked before it is replaced.
* ''Adding stops'': ''+ Object'' in the path panel adds the selected card or shape, or – with nothing selected – the cards and shapes you click next (Esc ends). ''Frame ▾'' adds the current view or lets you draw a frame. Renaming it there later keeps it tied to the story. Its `story` field holds the story's tiddlers in order (a title list, as in `[enlist{Story title!!story}]`) and `pinboard-levels` their indents; it shows them as an outline with an ''Open story'' button. A card stop brings its card; a frame stop brings every card lying inside the frame, even those that are not stops of their own. Both directions stay in step: reordering the stops or moving cards in and out of frames rewrites the field, and editing it elsewhere (a field editor, `<$action-listops $field="story">`) reorders, adds or removes card and chapter stops. Cards that are only there because of a frame follow the frame; move them on the board. Making a story tiddler creates no other tiddlers.
* ''Renaming'': with [[Relink|https://flibbles.github.io/tw5-relink/]] installed, renaming a tiddler anywhere in the wiki also renames it on every board: its card and stops, story and frame tiddlers, the board named by a story tiddler, and the `story` fields. Without Relink, a renamed card leaves the board.
* ''Frame entries'': a selected frame's ''Make an entry'' button gives it a tiddler of its own, named after the frame's text (field `pinboard-frame` names the board). In story tiddlers it becomes a chapter with the frame's cards indented below it, and its own `story` field lists the cards lying inside the frame (in story order, then top to bottom). Once made, the button opens it. Renaming the frame later does not rename its tiddler.
* ''Open story'' (gear or story tiddler) puts the story tiddler and its cards at the top of the story river, in order, and leaves the board's fullscreen.

Messages for buttons inside the graph: `graph-pinboard-present` (optional `step`), `graph-pinboard-fit`, `graph-pinboard-open` (`tiddler`), `graph-center-node` (`tiddler`), `graph-move-view` (`x`, `y`, `scale`, `scaleBy`).
